          "path": "_m/g/c/v/6/morton-castle-wp/morton-castle-geograph-org-uk--1.jpg",
          "filename": "Morton Castle - geograph.org.uk - 1106456.jpg",
          "caption": "Morton Castle Set in an attractive setting above Morton Loch the original castle dates from the 14th century, or earlier, although what is visible today is later in date. At the time of Robert the Bruce it was held by his lieutenant Thomas Randolph, then for a time by the English and later was given to the Douglas family as Earls of Morton. Located not far from the A702 road but approached by a narrow minor road it is largely passed unseen by tourists but well worthwhile deviating to visit.",
          "alt": "Morton Castle Set in an attractive setting above Morton Loch the original castle dates from the 14th century, or earlier, although what is visible today is later in date. At the time of Robert the Bruce it was held by his lieutenant Thomas Randolph, then for a time by the English and later was given to the Douglas family as Earls of Morton. Located not far from the A702 road but approached by a narrow minor road it is largely passed unseen by tourists but well worthwhile deviating to visit.",
